# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Raw and intermediate dataset files.
# NASA/CALCE raw exports are large and licence-restricted; see docs and
# configs/dataset_sources.yaml for where to obtain them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/raw/**/*.zip
data/raw/**/*.mat
data/raw/**/*.csv
data/raw/**/*.xlsx
data/raw/**/*.xls
data/raw/nasa/cleaned_dataset/
data/interim/**/*.csv
data/interim/**/*.parquet
data/processed/**/*.parquet

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GENERATED PIPELINE OUTPUTS (Batch 13).
#
# Everything below is rewritten wholesale by `python main.py` on simulated
# telemetry. Tracking it meant every pipeline run dirtied the working tree
# (behavior_features_v1.csv alone churns ~8k lines), which buried real
# uncommitted source changes in `git status` noise.
#
# Nothing reads these files back in: main.py passes the tables to the
# dashboard in-memory, and tests/test_pipeline.py asserts against a tmp_path
# output directory, not against these committed copies. Regenerate with
# `python main.py`.
#
# NOTE the deliberate asymmetry with reports/metrics/ below: only the two
# distribution CSVs there are main.py outputs. The rest are NASA-derived
# research artifacts and stay tracked -- see the block after this one.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/features/*.csv
data/processed/**/*.csv
!data/processed/calce/calce_sample_processed.csv
!data/processed/nasa/nasa_sample_processed.csv
reports/metrics/battery_state_distribution.csv
reports/metrics/risk_distribution.csv

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DELIBERATELY NOT IGNORED (Batch 13) -- do not "tidy" these away:
#
#   reports/metrics/*.csv  (all except the two named above)
#   reports/figures/*.png
#
# These are derived from the NASA cleaned_dataset (7.2M rows), which is
# gitignored above and not redistributable. They CANNOT be regenerated from a
# clean checkout. They are also live runtime inputs:
#
#   continuous_model_training_data.csv -> tests/test_adaptive_{validation,
#       datasets,calibrator,commensurability,dataset_specs}.py,
#       src/bms/adaptive/__main__.py, scripts/fit_{shap,horizon,mixed}*.py
#   calibration_merged.csv             -> tests/test_explain.py,
#       scripts/{validate_health_index_versions,audit_threshold_reachability}.py
#   nasa_ground_truth_fade.csv,
#   nasa_pipeline_scores.csv,
#   horizon_regression_summary.csv     -> scripts/generate_report_figures.py
#
# Ignoring them would break the test suite on a fresh clone and make
# docs/final_report.md and docs/calibration_report.md unreproducible.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Adaptive calibration runtime store (versions + decision log are run artifacts)
models/adaptive/
